---
export const prerender = true;

import Tutorial from "../../layouts/Tutorial.astro";
import { TOOL_COUNT } from "../../data/tools";
---

<Tutorial
  title="Use the free tools, no account needed - Laravel SEO Tutorials"
  description="A tour of the free Laravel SEO tools anyone can use without an account: website status, SSL, DNS, WHOIS, redirect checker, Lighthouse and the developer and content utilities."
  heading="Use the free tools, no account needed"
  intro={`The app ships with ${TOOL_COUNT} one-off tools that anyone can use straight from the browser. No signup, no API key: open the tool, paste a domain or some text, read the result.`}
>
  <h2>Find a tool</h2>
  <p>
    Everything lives at
    <a href="https://app.laravelseo.com/tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.laravelseo.com/tools</a>.
    The search box filters the list as you type, and the tools are grouped into <strong>Research</strong>,
    <strong>Developer</strong> and <strong>Content</strong>.
  </p>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/app/tools-index.png"
      alt="The tools index with its search box and the Research category"
      width="1280"
      height="720"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>The tools index: search plus three categories.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Example: is this site down for everyone?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the <a href="https://app.laravelseo.com/tools/website-status-checker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website status checker</a>.</li>
    <li>Type the domain, for example <code>laravelcompany.com</code>, and press <strong>Search</strong>.</li>
    <li>The result shows whether the site is online, the HTTP status code and how long it took to respond.</li>
  </ol>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/app/tool-website-status.png"
      alt="Website status checker result for laravelcompany.com: online, HTTP 200, 0.35 seconds"
      width="1280"
      height="720"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>laravelcompany.com: online, 200, 0.35 seconds.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Example: check a certificate before it expires</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the <a href="https://app.laravelseo.com/tools/ssl-checker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSL checker</a>.</li>
    <li>Enter the domain and press <strong>Search</strong>.</li>
    <li>You get the certificate status, issuer, signature algorithm and the exact issue and expiry dates.</li>
  </ol>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/app/tool-ssl-checker.png"
      alt="SSL checker result for laravelseo.com: valid certificate from Google Trust Services, expiring 2027-01-02"
      width="1280"
      height="720"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>laravelseo.com: valid certificate, with the expiry date spelled out.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Example: audit a page with Lighthouse</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://app.laravelseo.com/tools/lighthouse" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lighthouse SEO audit</a>
    runs Google Lighthouse against any URL and returns the scores and failing audits, without you installing anything.
  </p>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/app/tool-lighthouse.png"
      alt="The Lighthouse SEO audit tool, waiting for a URL"
      width="1280"
      height="720"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>Paste a URL, press Search, get the Lighthouse breakdown.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>The rest of the toolbox</h2>
  <p>
    DNS, WHOIS, IP and redirect checks sit next to developer utilities (minifiers, JSON validator, UTM builder,
    generators) and content helpers (word counter, slug converter, case converter and more). The full list with
    one-line descriptions is on the <a href="/tools">tools directory</a>.
  </p>
</Tutorial>
